//!
//! # Data layout
//!
//! A single `BlockfileReader<u32, SparsePostingBlock>` stores two kinds of
//! entries, distinguished by their string prefix:
//!
//! - **Posting data blocks** — prefix `encode_u32(dim)`, keys `0, 1, 2, …`.
//!   Each value is a `SparsePostingBlock` holding a contiguous, offset-sorted
//!   slice of the dimension's `(offset, weight)` posting list. When a
//!   dimension's entries do not fit in a single block (see
//!   [`MaxScoreWriter::with_block_size`]) they are split across several keys.
//!   Data blocks have `is_directory() == false`.
//!
//! - **Directory parts** — prefix `DIRECTORY_PREFIX + encode_u32(dim)`, keys
//!   `0, 1, 2, …`. Written only for dimensions with more than one data block.
//!   Each value is a directory [`SparsePostingBlock`] (`is_directory() ==
//!   true`) recording the `(max_offset, max_weight)` of each data block, used
//!   for block-max pruning.
//!
//! `DIRECTORY_PREFIX` (`"~"`) sorts after every base64-encoded dimension key,
